  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA-2000) achieves 48.5% acc / 46.4% F1, while config_010 (image-only, singleprofile, ResNet50) is very weak at 20.8% acc. RNA is clearly the dominant modality, and the PCA encoder is a simple linear baseline. Uncertainty: We do not know whether a learned nonlinear RNA encoder (scVI, 200-dim latent) can meaningfully improve over PCA, which is a fundamental representation question that will affect all downstream multimodal decisions. This experiment (config_004: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) isolates exactly one variable—RNA encoder—against the config_001 baseline, keeping profile setting and modality identical. If scVI substantially outperforms PCA, it justifies investing budget in scVI-based multimodal configs; if not, PCA remains the efficient choice and we can redirect exploration toward profile/aggregation or image-side improvements. Under a tight budget, this clean A/B comparison on the strongest modality maximizes information gained per experiment."
}

